  "reason": "The records collectively suggest several relevant ideas: cooling rate can kinetically retain metastable fcc structures (R4, R7), composition can control C14 formation (R2), and multiphase decomposition can affect coercivity in Co–Fe–Ni-containing HEAs (R3). Other records address thermal or compositional phase control in chemically related alloys. Thus an expert could be led toward combining rapid cooling with phase engineering to study magnetic coercivity. However, none identifies the specific FeCoNiTi fcc+C14 combination, the compositionally matched C14-rich comparator, Ti-sublattice antiferromagnetic coupling, phase-resolved transition temperatures, or orbital/spin-canting-assisted domain-wall pinning. Reconstructing the specific intervention and mechanism would therefore require substantial new insight."
